  "response_text": "A queue holds each new TCB at the back and always picks the front TCB when a time slice ends or a thread yields. After running, the thread\u2019s TCB goes back to the rear so every task takes turns in first-in, first-out order. Using a queue means you never worry about managing wrap-around indices or skipping inactive slots in an array. Enqueue and dequeue are both constant-time, so the scheduler stays simple and fair.\\n",
